{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And the covering</b> — the fat that covers the entrails, this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Leviticus 9:19). And it is not correct in my eyes, for why would Scripture mention this particular fat and not mention the other fats? But in my opinion, \"the covering\" is a name for all of them, for any fat that is offered upon the altar is a covering (מְכַסֶּה): the one is the fat that covers the entrails, and the second, all the fat that is upon the entrails — it too is a covering; and the fat that is upon the kidneys covers them, and likewise that which is upon the flanks, as they said (Ḥullin 93b): fat that the flesh covers over it is permitted — for regarding the flanks the Merciful One stated \"upon,\" and not what is within the flanks. Now this verse continues from above: \"And the sons of Aaron brought to him the blood\" — of the bull and the ram that were mentioned — \"and the fats from the bull\"; but from the ram they brought him the tail and the fat, and from both of them the kidneys and the appendage of the liver. And it says, <b>And they placed the fats upon the breasts</b>, because the tail and the kidneys and the appendage of the liver they would place below and the fats upon them, and all upon the breasts. Thus the fats alone would be seen on top, and this is a way of honor in the burning:"], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:52:03.678287131Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}